"{\"status\":\"changes_required\",\"reviewed_aspects\":[\"request_coverage\",\"lifecycle_and_progress\",\"payload_and_dependencies\",\"verification_consistency\",\"observation_sufficiency\",\"unresolved_assumptions\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"F_REFRESH_AND_CLEANUP_CANDIDATE_PATH_MISSING\",\"scope\":\"architecture\",\"message\":\"The only declared candidate-create event requires active ownership and explicitly excludes selected refresh preparation/service. After a READ/WRITE retires, close-page cleanup has no active request, and refresh preparation also operates after active work drains. No separate event, handshake, or update rule defines creation of the required cleanup PRE candidates or refresh-preparation PRE/REF candidates. Consequently, the required close-page maintenance and refresh drain/close/REF progress paths cannot be implemented from the declared lifecycle without violating the candidate-create contract. Define explicit architecture-level candidate-creation/control paths for cleanup and refresh preparation, including their priority relative to active work, blocked-candidate holding, commit, and dispatch, while preserving the locked system behavior.\",\"references\":[\"/context/documents/shared/events/candidate_create\",\"/context/documents/execution/rules/EXEC_CLEANUP\",\"/context/documents/execution/rules/EXEC_REFRESH\",\"/context/documents/modules/contracts/command_engine/owned_state\",\"/context/documents/modules/contracts/command_engine/update_events\",\"/context/documents/modules/contracts/command_engine/handshakes/candidate\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"R7\",\"R8\",\"R12\",\"BASE_SEQUENCE\",\"BASE_POLICY\",\"BASE_REFRESH\"]},{\"id\":\"F_PROBE_PAYLOAD_NOT_OBSERVABLE\",\"scope\":\"architecture\",\"message\":\"The payload requirements require probe_command to remain the independently defined first-command query even when probe_valid is low, including under idle, cleanup, refresh, and reset gating. The verification bindings expose neither probe_command nor probe_valid as observations, and the payload checks list only candidate and commit payload observations. cmd_ready alone cannot distinguish an incorrect probe payload from a correct payload that is merely invalid or not permitted. Bind probe_command and probe_valid to declared observations and include them in the payload checks so the valid-low probe-payload exception is verifiable.\",\"references\":[\"/context/documents/execution/rules/EXEC_PAYLOAD\",\"/context/documents/modules/contracts/command_engine/interfaces/probe_command\",\"/context/documents/modules/contracts/command_engine/interfaces/probe_valid\",\"/context/documents/verification/checks/execution.verification.X_PAYLOAD\",\"/context/documents/verification/checks/system.verification.V_PAYLOAD\",\"/context/documents/verification/observations\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"R13\"]},{\"id\":\"F_TIMING_PROFILE_ASSUMPTION_UNRESOLVED\",\"scope\":\"system\",\"message\":\"The selected DDR4-3200 timing values are necessary to implement and verify tRCD, tRAS, tRP, tRRD, tFAW, tREFI, and tRFC, but the package marks availability of the selected timing-library paths as requiring review. Until that external timing-library assumption is resolved, the numeric source used for mandatory timing and refresh behavior is not approved for RTL generation. Review and resolve the declared timing-profile source assumption before downstream decomposition or implementation; do not alter the locked selected profile or timing requirements as an architecture-only repair.\",\"references\":[\"/package/assumptions/A_PROFILE\",\"/context/documents/shared/timing_profile\",\"/context/documents/shared/timing_rules\",\"/package/timing_library/DDR4-3200\"],\"requirement_ids\":[\"R5\",\"R8\",\"BASE_TIMING\",\"BASE_TRRD\",\"BASE_TFAW\",\"BASE_REFRESH\"]}]}"
